{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"40659144c078fae3396368780526451b8c97500ffc92fc5b42a0d6e66c449941","digest":{"component_or_area":"push entrypoint and lock-artifact exclusion","key_entities":["src/rebar/_store/push.py","_ignore_lock_artifacts","info/exclude",".ticket-write.lock",".ticket-write.lock.d/","os.write","O_APPEND","O_WRONLY","tests/unit/test_commit_and_push_tickets_branch_heldout.py","PushDeliveryError","stage-failed"],"problem_keywords":["lock-artifact exclusion","concurrent write safety","metadata corruption","POSIX atomicity","failure coverage"],"propositions":["Buffered two-write append to info/exclude can interleave under concurrent first use and tear a pattern into a corrupt half-line, silently disabling lock-artifact exclusion.","The exclusion-write and git status failure gates lack direct test coverage for both strict and default failure modes and their recovery paths.","Exclusion metadata corruption and failure outcomes must be hardened while preserving the compatibility contract that duplicate whole lines are acceptable and deliberate.","A single atomic os.write to an O_APPEND descriptor on POSIX eliminates byte-level interleaving hazards and must be proven by concurrent integrity and real-commit artifact-absence tests."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787356969160267001,"uuid":"1354de51-70ff-4fbf-886d-72787099fa68"}